<title>
DTC P0197 / P0198
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
There are two types of OBD system on ECM depending on the vehicle specification.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
For identification, refer to “Discrimination for OBD System” under 
<intxref refid = "AENLJA0A1121003">OBD System Description:K12C</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<servinfosub id = "AENLJA0A1124030001">
<title>
DTC Detecting Condition and Trouble Area
</title>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "3.598in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "3.598in"/>
<thead>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "1" valign = "middle" align = "center">
<ptxt>
DTC detecting condition
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "1" valign = "middle" align = "center">
<ptxt>
Trouble area
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "1" valign = "top" align = "left">
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
P0197: Engine Oil Temperature Sensor Circuit Low
</emph>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Output voltage of oil temperature sensor signal circuit is lower than 0.02 V for 5 sec.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
(3 D/C detection logic (type A) but MIL does not light up)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
(2 D/C detection logic (type B) but MIL does not light up)
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" morerows = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "1" valign = "top" align = "left">
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil temperature sensor and/or its circuit
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
ECM
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "1" valign = "top" align = "left">
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
P0198: Engine Oil Temperature Sensor Circuit High
</emph>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Output voltage of oil temperature sensor signal circuit is higher than 4.65 V for 5 sec.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
(3 D/C detection logic (type A) but MIL does not light up)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
(2 D/C detection logic (type B) but MIL does not light up)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
